<p>The U.S. government announced sanctions Monday against three people and nine companies accused of helping Iran sell and ship oil to China, including four companies based in Hong Kong, four in the United Arab Emirates and one in Oman. The Treasury Department said the designations target individuals and entities that helped Iran&#x27;s Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps use front companies in permissive jurisdictions to move oil and route proceeds to Tehran. The measures follow sanctions announced Friday against people and companies accused of aiding Iranian purchases of weapons and components used to make drones and ballistic missiles. Several accounts said the action came before President Trump&#x27;s expected trip to China and planned meeting with Chinese President Xi Jinping, where the Iran confrontation and the Strait of Hormuz were expected to be on the agenda. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said the Trump administration would keep increasing pressure on Tehran to deny Iran&#x27;s government and military funding for weapons development, its nuclear program and regional proxies.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ybsjuA6TDQzSZyF21iK6b46mXDWjv_2PWw5sHgcnBm9F56mV4jC7lBV7kl6BMfZAs65Mue3sI7yNux3bfJTfpuBRBqoRt-mxZUAsye-KfmMFlf8wnH0Ie45OAXrVgyXY2h7X3gadGqs2fzVSHujU_clJ1oowGnuNnVUt62cK3v-J4VCm3Gf2zVM9cqAWsN66tCVmFCWqGLU0c8S7AjfHfQi7PtZcNIzfUMzJtIW9FfosDDgdOzpM9n5jN_HVvG8COg_EAw' alt='Donald Trump speaks with Chinese President Xi Jinping as they shake hands after a meeting at Gimhae Air Base.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Named firms: Listed companies included Hong Kong Blue Ocean Ltd, Hong Kong Sanmu Ltd, Jiandi HK Ltd, Max Honor International Trade Co Ltd, Ocean Allianz Shipping LLC, Atic Energy FZE, Zeus Logistics, Blanca LLC and Universal Fortune Trading LLC.</li><li>Asset freeze: The designations block any property the targeted people and companies hold under U.S. jurisdiction and prohibit U.S. persons and entities from transacting with them.</li><li>Reward offer: The U.S. State Department offered up to $15 million for information that helps disrupt the IRGC&#x27;s financial mechanisms and related networks.</li><li>Named officials: Haber7 identified Ahmed Muhammedi Zade as head of the IRGC&#x27;s Shahid Pourjafari oil branch, Samed Fethi Salami as finance chief for foreign-exchange transactions and Muhammedrıza Eşrefi Gehi as trade chief.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Brett Erickson, Obsidian Risk Advisors: Erickson said the Treasury actions were aimed at curbing Iran&#x27;s ability to threaten ships operating in the Strait of Hormuz and regional allies. (<a href='https://minutemirror.com.pk/us-imposes-sanctions-on-12-individuals-and-entities-over-irans-oil-shipments-to-china-554258/'>Minute Mirror</a>)</li><li>Naewna: The Thai outlet tied the sanctions to wider concern over China&#x27;s role in the conflict, citing reports that Beijing might be preparing to provide Iran with new air-defense systems. (<a href='https://www.naewna.com/inter/963875'>Naewna</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/us-issues-new-sanctions-over-iran%27s-oil-shipments-to-china4'>U.S. issues new sanctions over Iran&#x27;s oil shipments to China</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-issues-new-sanctions-over-irans-oil-shipments-to-china/article70968108.ece'>U.S. issues new sanctions over Iran’s oil shipments to China</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/05/us-issues-new-sanctions-over-irans-oil-shipments-china'>US issues new sanctions over Iran&#x27;s oil shipments to China</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-sanctions-12-iran-linked-individuals-entities-over-china-oil-sales-11481527#publisher=newsstand'>US Sanctions 12 Iran-Linked Individuals, Entities Over China Oil Sales</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/us-issue